WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.009
It shows you where the trouble is.

3
00:00:04.709 --> 00:00:08.822
You hold the grown-up page. Your child gets the page with the big words.

4
00:00:09.272 --> 00:00:10.450
There are three parts.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.832
Part A. Your child reads the sixteen words, one at a time. Mark each one that is read right.

6
00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:24.531
Part B. Your child reads three sentences. The same words are inside them. Mark only the words your page shows.

7
00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:28.621
Part C. Six short words to sound out. Slow is fine here.

8
00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:32.743
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just listen and mark.

9
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:38.910
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

10
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:45.482
It may show that the real trouble is sounding out. Then a different plan comes first, and your page names it.

11
00:00:45.932 --> 00:00:50.344
It may show that the words are known on a card, but lost inside a sentence.

12
00:00:50.794 --> 00:00:54.575
Or that very few are known yet. Or that some stay and some slip away.

13
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:58.871
Each line tells you which days to do, and which job matters most.

14
00:00:59.321 --> 00:01:03.999
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
